# Prompt
You are the openspec specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase ui_and_review, story SKY-006-B.
NOTE: This story has 15 acceptance criteria — MANDATORY split required (see SPLIT RULES below).

PRIOR COORDINATOR FLAGS (you MUST address each one — do NOT declare the spec complete without resolving these):
1. CRITICAL: AC-9 (dependency-guard precondition) references heading names ('## Project Structure', '## Dependencies', '## Code Quality', '## Test Coverage', '## Security') that do not match SKY-006-A-1 AC-2 headings ('## TypeScript', '## Tests', '## Security', '## Error Handling', '## Express Safety', '## Verdict') — implementation will always abort with prerequisite failure; heading names must be reconciled before implementation
2. AC count is 15 at splitDepth=1 — exceeds 12-AC limit; split rules cannot fire at splitDepth=1; human decision required on consolidation
3. Coverage floor default of 80% (AC-3) was added by openspec without explicit human policy sign-off — requires human confirmation
4. Split child from a split that contradicts coordinator routing — requires parent-level human confirmation before implementation
5. AC-8 document structure self-check references 'SKY-006-A AC-2' by cross-story reference — creates a maintenance dependency; heading list should be inlined

Additional context from prior review: Both openspec and speckit contributed genuine, non-overlapping value in the second run. openspec resolved the critical Verdict format inconsistency (unified to ^(PASS|FAIL)$ as first non-blank line), fixed the section-count contradiction in AC-7 (corrected 'exactly six' to 'exactly eight'), added GATE-ASYNC-EXPRESS-ERROR (EH_EXPRESS_NEXT_ERR), formalized CORS as EXPRESS_CORS with explicit pass/fail criteria, added 80% default coverage floor, and added named gate identifiers throughout. speckit t

Generate refined acceptance criteria, optionally updated title/description, and split stories where required. Output JSON only between <SPEC_AGENT> tags using this schema:
{
  "storyId":"SKY-006-B",
  "agent":"openspec",
  "notes":"context",
  "acceptanceCriteria":["..."],
  "description":"...",
  "title":"...",
  "splitStories":[{"id":"optional","title":"...","description":"...","acceptanceCriteria":["..."],"agentRole":"...","technicalNotes":{"files":[]}}]
}
Use existing text when no change is needed.

SPLIT RULES (mandatory, not optional — enforce these before refining AC):
1. AC count > 12 → you MUST propose a split. Target ≤8 ACs per split child. Never leave a story with >12 ACs unsplit.
2. Both implementation files AND test files in technicalNotes.files → split into one impl child (non-test files) and one test child (*.test.ts files). Assign agentRole "typescript-engineer" to impl, "test-engineer" to test.
3. 3+ independent deliverable modules with no shared exports (e.g. client.ts, server.ts, cli.ts all in same story) → split per concern. Each split gets the files it owns.
4. External API discovery + implementation in same story → split: first child discovers/documents the API contract, second child implements against that contract.
These rules apply only when splitDepth === 0. Never split a story that is already a split child.

